    <string name="sg_faq_use_q">How do I use a template?</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_use_a">Turn on the ScriptGo keyboard, then in a chat type the trigger (usually /) followed by the shortcut, for example /ongkir. Pick the template from the suggestions. You can also hold the space bar to open the template list.</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_keyboard_q">The ScriptGo keyboard does not show up. Why?</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_keyboard_a">Open Keyboard settings from the Account tab, turn on ScriptGo, then choose ScriptGo as your keyboard. In a chat you can also switch keyboards with the keyboard icon at the bottom of the screen.</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_variables_q">Why are {nama} or {kota} not filled in?</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_variables_a">Values come from the contact you pick when using a template. Make sure the contact has that data, or give a fallback in the field (Fields tab) or in the template, for example {kota|Bandung}.</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_privacy_q">Does ScriptGo read what I type?</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_privacy_a">No. The keyboard never sends or stores what you type. Only the templates, contacts, and fields you create are synced, and only when you sign in.</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_laptop_q">Can I use it on a laptop?</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_laptop_a">Yes. Install the ScriptGo Chrome extension and sign in with the same account. Your templates and contacts are there right away, including on WhatsApp Web.</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_password_q">Forgot your password?</string>
    <string name="sg_faq_password_a">Just sign in with an email code: choose Continue with email, then enter the 6-digit code from your email. Then you can create a new password in Account → Password.</string>
